        "original_id": "ec84fafe-180a-5fda-a76e-1c8f86dde248",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: California, southeastern California, Yuma, Arizona, Colorado River, Calexico, Imperial Valley\n- Systems: Madera Canal, All-American Canal, Imperial Dam\n\nFacts:\n- The Madera Canal is a 35.9-mile aqueduct in California.\n- The All-American Canal is an 80-mile aqueduct in southeastern California.\n- Imperial Dam is about 30 miles northeast of Yuma, Arizona on the Colorado River.\n- Imperial Dam diverts water into the All-American Canal.\n- The All-American Canal runs to just west of Calexico, California before its last branch heads mostly north into the Imperial Valley.",
